                <pb facs="0140" n="1100" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1100"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 240.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Crain to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >House of Representatives</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 9,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to submit for your
                    consideration the inclosed communication from Mr. J. J. Cocke, collector of
                    customs of the district of Brazos Santiago, in the State of Texas, in which he
                    forcibly presents reasons why there ought to be a treaty between Mexico and the
                    United States for the purpose of establishing the boundary between the two
                    countries.</p>
                <p>Your early attention to this subject is earnestly invoked.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. H. Crain.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
